if(window.deepArticles["panamanian-military-regime"]){
  Object.assign(window.deepArticles["panamanian-military-regime"],{
    lead:"<!-- altwwii-writer-block:start id=wb-g-20260815-c3j7z writer=g kind=revision created=2026-08-15T23:42:00-06:00 --><strong>The Panamanian military regime</strong> is the nationalist security order established from 1968. Its fixed functions are military-backed government, canal nationalism without canal recovery, American security cooperation, developmental administration, and intelligence brokerage. The historical Torrijos–Noriega sequence is a working implementation, not fixed leadership canon.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='a'>[a]</sup><!-- altwwii-writer-block:end -->",
    canon:"<!-- altwwii-writer-block:start id=wb-g-20260815-d4k8a writer=g kind=revision created=2026-08-15T23:42:00-06:00 -->The 1968 military regime, continued American strategic control, later defense expansion, security cooperation, and counting-house economy are established through the mid-1980s.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='a'>[a]</sup> Historical coup leadership, Torrijos's rule and death, Noriega's rise, civilian constitutional forms, and the Canal Partnership Accord are developed working continuity. Exact leaders, coup sequence, elections, offices, treaty names, and dates remain open.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='e'>[e]</sup><!-- altwwii-writer-block:end -->",
    facts:[["Beginning","1968 · exact coup sequence open"],["Founding armed institution","Exact title open"],["Working initial coup leader","Boris Martínez"],["Working principal leader","Omar Torrijos"],["Working later intelligence ruler","Manuel Noriega"],["Working canal settlement","Canal Partnership Accord"],["Canal defense command","United States"],["Government form","Military command with civilian offices"]]
  });
}
replacePanamaSection("panamanian-military-regime","rupture","<!-- altwwii-writer-block:start id=wb-g-20260815-e5l9b writer=g kind=revision created=2026-08-15T23:42:00-06:00 --><p>The regime begins in 1968. The historical route has the National Guard depose Arnulfo Arias on 11 October, Boris Martínez initiate the seizure, and Torrijos displace the first commanders in 1969. These names and dates remain working continuity pending the exact coup and ruler sequence.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='e'>[e]</sup></p><!-- altwwii-writer-block:end -->");
replacePanamaSection("panamanian-military-regime","government","<!-- altwwii-writer-block:start id=wb-g-20260815-f6m2c writer=g kind=revision created=2026-08-15T23:42:00-06:00 --><p>The regime governs through its armed institution, civilian offices, social programs, and controlled representation. The developed historical route assigns developmental leadership to Torrijos and later intelligence rule to <a href='manuel-noriega.html'>Manuel Noriega</a>. Exact leaders, constitutional forms, succession, and dates remain open.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='e'>[e]</sup></p><!-- altwwii-writer-block:end -->");
replacePanamaSection("panamanian-military-regime","canal","<!-- altwwii-writer-block:start id=wb-g-20260815-g7n3d writer=g kind=revision created=2026-08-15T23:42:00-06:00 --><p>The regime turns the martyrs of 1964 into a negotiating program but never receives the canal. A working <a href='canal-partnership-accord.html'>Partnership Accord</a> expands revenue, employment, jurisdiction, development, and nonmilitary land while leaving American powers intact; exact settlement name and provisions remain open.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='e'>[e]</sup></p><!-- altwwii-writer-block:end -->");
replacePanamaSection("panamanian-military-regime","security","<!-- altwwii-writer-block:start id=wb-g-20260815-h8p4e writer=g kind=revision created=2026-08-15T23:42:00-06:00 --><p>The armed institution and its intelligence directorate monitor canal labor, opposition, foreign agents, shipping, banks, and the Colombian frontier. American services value the network for canal security and regional reporting, giving the regime leverage without strategic independence. Calling the institution the National Guard and its broker Noriega remains working continuity.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='e'>[e]</sup></p><!-- altwwii-writer-block:end -->");
replacePanamaSection("panamanian-military-regime","economy","<p>The <a href='panamanian-transit-financial-economy.html'>transit and financial economy</a> expands through canal traffic, shipping registries, warehouses, banks, insurers, customs brokers, construction, and corporate subsidiaries. Protected by American strategy and Panamanian secrecy, the country becomes a proxy counting house rather than a principal proxy battlefield.</p>");
